# === Cave-survey data (never commit user survey data) ==================
# Survey snapshots anywhere (runs/, work files). Tracked ground truth is the
# JSON inspector reports + RUNLOG.md / log.md / SESSIONS.md — keep those.
*.csz
*.CSZ
*.csx
*.CSX

# Bulky gitignored reference material migrated from cSurvey/dev
# (present locally, absent from a fresh clone; see feature README)
features/*/literature/
features/*/example/

# === SB <-> satellite sync runs (features/*/sb-sync) ====================
# One dated folder per `cavedossier sat sync --out` run. The lists carry real
# society data (cave names, field comments, coordinates), and a run is a
# snapshot of two moving sources — re-run rather than reuse. The README that
# explains the folder is tracked; nothing a run produces is.
features/*/sb-sync/*
!features/*/sb-sync/README.md

# === Secrets / per-machine config =======================================
.env

# === Excel lock files + workbook backups ================================
~$*
*.backup.xlsm
*.backup.xlsx

# === Python =============================================================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# === OS / editor cruft ==================================================
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# === OSZ template workbench (features/cave-dossier/osz-template) =========
# Word autosave leftovers (~$ lock files are covered above)
~WRL*.tmp
# Same-day template iterations: heavy, near-identical .docx; the current
# template in templates/ is the tracked one
features/cave-dossier/osz-template/templates/archive/
# Generated mockups: regenerate with tools/make_mockup.py — only the PDFs
# (small, reviewable without Word) stay tracked
features/cave-dossier/osz-template/mockups/*.docx

# === Auto-commit hook (.claude/hooks/auto-commit.sh) =====================
# Per-machine run log; the commits themselves are the tracked record
.claude/auto-commit.log

# Distribution copies are byte-identical to templates/ — the tracked pair there
# (Zapisnik_OSZ_v10.dotx + _gdocs.docx) is the record of what was handed out
features/cave-dossier/osz-template/distribution/
